```cpp
#include <array>
#include <string>
#include <vector>

int main() {
    std::array<int, 7> daily_steps{};           // exactly 7, fixed at compile time.
    daily_steps.at(6) = 9000;                   // at(): bounds-checked.

    std::vector<int> scores;
    scores.reserve(100);                        // capacity 100: no reallocation below it.
    scores.push_back(71);
    int& first = scores[0];                     // safe while size <= 100.
    for (int i = 0; i < 50; ++i) scores.push_back(i);
    first += 1;                                 // still valid: no reallocation happened.

    std::string name = "Asha";
    name += " Rao";                            // grows like a vector of chars.
    std::size_t n = name.size();                // 8.
    (void)n;
}
```

| Need | Choose |
|---|---|
| fixed count known at compile time. | `std::array`. |
| size changes at run time. | `std::vector`. |
| text. | `std::string`. |
| stable references while growing. | reserve, or store indexes. |

